; C8  Winning 42 p. 54 (W42-p054-c) and p. 49 (W42-p049-a)
; Rule, in our words: a setter following the bidder's double, holding a count
; tile of the led suit and another tile of it, follows with a tile that is not
; count. (The book's reading of the converse, that a setter who follows the
; double with count has no more of the suit, needs the record of an earlier
; trick: GAPS.md, history and policy likelihood.)
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c8): a setter, the bidder led a non-trump
; double, the mover holds a count follower and two or more followers; the
; book's tiles are the non-count followers.
; How this encoding differs: none from the gate. The book's own instances are
; on trump doubles (Hands 33 and 35, pp. 111, 116), which the gate excludes.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0.
(policy c08-no-count-on-the-double
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule follow-without-count (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair me) (domino doubled) (domino plain) (domino count-tile) (context led))
        (out plain)
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (opponent me S0)
          (leader S0)
          (trick-play S0 doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (in doubled q*))
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal plain)
          (in plain led)
          (count plain 0)
          (own-legal count-tile)
          (in count-tile led)
          (count count-tile 5))
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (opponent me S0)
          (leader S0)
          (trick-play S0 doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (in doubled q*))
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal plain)
          (in plain led)
          (count plain 0)
          (own-legal count-tile)
          (in count-tile led)
          (count count-tile 10))))))
